title: FizzBuzz
golf: 60

Write `fizzbuzz(n)` that returns "Fizz" if n divides by 3, "Buzz" if it divides by 5,
"FizzBuzz" if it divides by both, and otherwise the number as a string (`"7"`).
=== starter
def fizzbuzz(n):
    ...
=== broken
def fizzbuzz(n):
    if n % 3 == 0:
        return "Fizz"
    elif n % 5 == 0:
        return "Buzz"
    elif n % 15 == 0:
        return "FizzBuzz"
    return str(n)
=== test
from harness import eq


def test_fizzbuzz(sol):
    eq(sol.fizzbuzz(9), "Fizz", "fizzbuzz(9)")
    eq(sol.fizzbuzz(10), "Buzz", "fizzbuzz(10)")
    eq(sol.fizzbuzz(30), "FizzBuzz", "fizzbuzz(30)")
    eq(sol.fizzbuzz(7), "7", "fizzbuzz(7)")
